import Mettapedia.TypeTheory.BubbleConversion
import Mettapedia.Logic.TheoryModel.Weakness
import Mettapedia.Logic.TheoryModel.DegenerateTop

/-!
# The weakness order of conversion bubbles

A bubble's definitional equality is a theory: its declared steps, read as
equations between expressions of the dependent comparison core.  Its strict
models are the congruences of the core's term algebra in which those equations
hold on the nose (`Congruence`, `strictSat`).  This file instantiates the
theory–model Galois connection with that satisfaction relation.

**Completeness.**  A bubble's conversion is exactly the semantic consequence of
its steps over strict models (`convertible_iff_entails`): sound in every strict
model, and complete because the conversion is itself a strict model
(`conversionModel`).  The closed theory of a bubble is its conversion
(`consequences_equations`), and its typing is global typing followed by one
equation valid in every strict model (`hasTypeIn_iff_models`).  This is the
congruence form of the equational consequence of
`Mettapedia.Logic.TheoryModel.Forgetting`, whose interpretations need not
respect term formers and whose consequence is the equivalence closure.

**The weakness order.**  One bubble has a smaller class of strict models than
another exactly when it converts at least as much (`models_equations_subset_iff`).
So every monotone measure of model classes, Bennett's count included, is
antitone in conversion (`weaknessOf_le_of_convertible`).  The global judgment
declares no step; every congruence is a strict model of it (`models_noSteps`),
so it has maximal weakness (`global_weakest`), strictly above every bubble that
converts two distinct expressions: the syntactic model separates them
(`models_ssubset_noSteps`).

**Strict against propositional.**  If every step of a bubble already holds in a
class of intended models (its justification by the global equality), adding
the bubble to the theory of that class leaves its models unchanged
(`justified_bubble_propositionally_invisible`), while the bubble's strict models
are strictly fewer than the global judgment's.  Weakness in this sense lives in
the judgmental theory, not in the propositional one.

**Weakest sufficient bubble.**  The weakest theory meeting a set of required
conversions is the conversion generated by exactly those requirements
(`isWeakestAdmissible_obligations`).  For a program, the requirements are its
conversion obligations: from the global type of each term to the type the
program asks for (`obligations`).  The bubble declaring exactly the obligations
types the program (`obligationBubble_types`), and every bubble that types the
program has no more strict models (`obligationBubble_weakest`).

**The degenerate model.**  The congruence relating everything (`total`) is the
unique strict model of the theory of all equations (`models_univ_eq_total`): the
inconsistent top of an equational language still has a model, and that model
identifies everything.

**Every type inhabited.**  Read beside the conversion language, the theory that
every expression of the core names an inhabited type changes no conversion
consequence of a bubble (`conversion_unchanged_by_inhabitation_top`), although
it entails that the empty proposition is inhabited
(`inhabitation_top_inhabits_bot`).  Collapsing the logic does not collapse
conversion.

**Controls** (on the arithmetic bubbles): a program needing `Vec 0 = Vec (0 + 0)`
is typed by the recursion equations and by the left-unit equation alone, whose
strict model classes are incomparable, so within that two-bubble family no
weakest sufficient bubble exists; the obligation bubble is strictly weaker than
both.  The obligation bubble of a program with a free variable is not stable
under substitution: it converts `Vec n` and `Vec (n + 0)` but not their
instances at `n := 0` (`obligation_not_substitution_stable`), while the
recursion equations are stable (`Arith.rule_stable`).

Scope: strict models here are congruences of the raw expression syntax of the
core, with binders as ordinary term formers.  Models of a full judgmental
theory (categories with families with strict equations) are not formalized.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Mettapedia.TypeTheory.BubbleWeakness

open Set
open Mettapedia.Logic.TheoryModel
open Mettapedia.TypeTheory.BubbleConversion
open Mettapedia.Logic.HOL
open Mettapedia.Logic.HOL.Embedding.SimpleSliceOfDependent
open Expr

universe u v uW

section Core

variable {Base : Type u} {Const : Ty Base → Type v}

/-! ## Conversion is a congruence -/

/-- A one-hole context that every rewrite step crosses carries conversions. -/
theorem convertible_context {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    (context : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const)
    (crosses : ∀ {a a' : Expr Base Const},
      Rewrite rules a a' → Rewrite rules (context a) (context a'))
    {a a' : Expr Base Const} (converted : Convertible rules a a') :
    Convertible rules (context a) (context a') := by
  induction converted with
  | rel _ _ step => exact Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (crosses step)
  | refl _ => exact Relation.EqvGen.refl _
  | symm _ _ _ ih => exact Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _ ih
  | trans _ _ _ _ _ ihFirst ihSecond => exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ ihFirst ihSecond

/-- A rewrite step whose root instances are conversions is a conversion: the
conversion of a bubble is closed under every term former. -/
theorem convertible_of_rewrite_convertible {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {e e' : Expr Base Const} (step : Rewrite (Convertible rules) e e') :
    Convertible rules e e' := by
  induction step with
  | root converted => exact converted
  | @piDomain A A' B _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => pi x B) .piDomain ih
  | @piBody A B B' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => pi A x) .piBody ih
  | @lamDomain A A' b _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => lam x b) .lamDomain ih
  | @lamBody A b b' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => lam A x) .lamBody ih
  | @appFunction f f' a _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => app x a) .appFunction ih
  | @appArgument f a a' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => app f x) .appArgument ih
  | @andLeft p p' q _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.and x q) .andLeft ih
  | @andRight p q q' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.and p x) .andRight ih
  | @orLeft p p' q _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.or x q) .orLeft ih
  | @orRight p q q' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.or p x) .orRight ih
  | @impLeft p p' q _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => imp x q) .impLeft ih
  | @impRight p q q' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => imp p x) .impRight ih
  | @notBody p p' _ ih => exact convertible_context Expr.not .notBody ih
  | @eqLeft a a' b _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.eq x b) .eqLeft ih
  | @eqRight a b b' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => Expr.eq a x) .eqRight ih
  | @allDomain A A' b _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => all x b) .allDomain ih
  | @allBody A b b' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => all A x) .allBody ih
  | @exDomain A A' b _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => ex x b) .exDomain ih
  | @exBody A b b' _ ih => exact convertible_context (fun x => ex A x) .exBody ih

/-! ## Strict models -/

/-- A strict model of the core's definitional equality, recorded by the
identifications it makes: an equivalence on expressions closed under every
term former.  Two interpretations of the core that identify the same
expressions are the same strict model. -/
structure Congruence (Base : Type u) (Const : Ty Base → Type v) where
  /-- The expressions the model identifies. -/
  rel : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop
  equivalence : Equivalence rel
  compatible : ∀ {e e' : Expr Base Const}, Rewrite rel e e' → rel e e'

@[ext]
theorem Congruence.ext {θ θ' : Congruence Base Const} (same : θ.rel = θ'.rel) : θ = θ' := by
  cases θ
  cases θ'
  cases same
  rfl

/-- An equation holds in a strict model when the model identifies its two sides. -/
def strictSat (θ : Congruence Base Const) (φ : Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const) : Prop :=
  θ.rel φ.1 φ.2

/-- The declared steps of a bubble, read as equations. -/
def equations (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    Set (Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const) :=
  {φ | rules φ.1 φ.2}

/-- **Soundness**: a strict model of a bubble's steps identifies every
conversion of the bubble. -/
theorem rel_of_convertible {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {θ : Congruence Base Const} (model : θ ∈ models strictSat (equations rules))
    {e e' : Expr Base Const} (converted : Convertible rules e e') : θ.rel e e' := by
  induction converted with
  | rel _ _ step =>
      exact θ.compatible (rewrite_mono (fun left right rule =>
        (model (show (left, right) ∈ equations rules from rule) : θ.rel left right)) step)
  | refl e => exact θ.equivalence.refl e
  | symm _ _ _ ih => exact θ.equivalence.symm ih
  | trans _ _ _ _ _ ihFirst ihSecond => exact θ.equivalence.trans ihFirst ihSecond

/-- The strict model given by a bubble's own conversion. -/
def conversionModel (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    Congruence Base Const where
  rel := Convertible rules
  equivalence := Relation.EqvGen.is_equivalence _
  compatible := convertible_of_rewrite_convertible

theorem conversionModel_mem (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    conversionModel rules ∈ models strictSat (equations rules) :=
  fun _ rule => Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root rule)

/-- **Completeness**: a bubble's conversion is exactly the semantic consequence
of its steps over strict models. -/
theorem convertible_iff_entails {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {e e' : Expr Base Const} :
    Convertible rules e e' ↔ Entails strictSat (equations rules) (e, e') :=
  ⟨fun converted _ model => rel_of_convertible model converted,
    fun entails => entails (conversionModel_mem rules)⟩

/-- The closed theory of a bubble is its conversion. -/
theorem consequences_equations (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    theoryOf strictSat (models strictSat (equations rules)) =
      {φ : Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const | Convertible rules φ.1 φ.2} :=
  Set.ext fun _ => convertible_iff_entails.symm

/-- The strict models of a bubble are the congruences containing its
conversion. -/
theorem mem_models_equations {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {θ : Congruence Base Const} :
    θ ∈ models strictSat (equations rules) ↔
      ∀ e e' : Expr Base Const, Convertible rules e e' → θ.rel e e' :=
  ⟨fun model _ _ converted => rel_of_convertible model converted,
    fun contains φ rule => contains φ.1 φ.2 (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root rule))⟩

/-- **Typing in a bubble, read in its strict models**: global typing followed by
an equation that every strict model of the bubble validates. -/
theorem hasTypeIn_iff_models {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {Γ : List (Expr Base Const)} {e B : Expr Base Const} :
    HasTypeIn rules Γ e B ↔
      ∃ A, HasType Γ e A ∧ ∀ θ ∈ models strictSat (equations rules), θ.rel A B := by
  rw [hasTypeIn_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨A, typing, converted⟩
    exact ⟨A, typing, fun _ model => rel_of_convertible model converted⟩
  · rintro ⟨A, typing, valid⟩
    exact ⟨A, typing, valid _ (conversionModel_mem rules)⟩

/-! ## The weakness order -/

/-- **The weakness order of bubbles reverses their conversion order**: the
strict models of `large` are among those of `small` exactly when `large`
converts everything `small` converts. -/
theorem models_equations_subset_iff {small large : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop} :
    models strictSat (equations large) ⊆ models strictSat (equations small) ↔
      ∀ e e' : Expr Base Const, Convertible small e e' → Convertible large e e' := by
  constructor
  · intro included e e' converted
    exact mem_models_equations.mp (included (conversionModel_mem large)) e e' converted
  · intro contained θ model
    exact mem_models_equations.mpr fun e e' converted =>
      rel_of_convertible model (contained e e' converted)

/-- Every monotone measure of strict model classes is antitone in conversion. -/
theorem weaknessOf_le_of_convertible {W : Type uW} [Preorder W]
    {μ : Set (Congruence Base Const) → W} (monotone : MonotoneMeasure μ)
    {small large : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    (contained : ∀ e e' : Expr Base Const, Convertible small e e' → Convertible large e e') :
    weaknessOf strictSat μ (equations large) ≤ weaknessOf strictSat μ (equations small) :=
  monotone (models_equations_subset_iff.mpr contained)

/-- The rule set of the global judgment: no declared step. -/
def noSteps : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop :=
  fun _ _ => False

/-- Every congruence is a strict model of the global judgment. -/
theorem models_noSteps :
    models strictSat (equations (noSteps : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop)) = Set.univ :=
  eq_univ_of_forall fun _ _ rule => False.elim rule

/-- **The global judgment has maximal weakness** for every monotone measure. -/
theorem global_weakest {W : Type uW} [Preorder W] {μ : Set (Congruence Base Const) → W}
    (monotone : MonotoneMeasure μ) (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    weaknessOf strictSat μ (equations rules) ≤ weaknessOf strictSat μ (equations noSteps) := by
  unfold weaknessOf
  rw [models_noSteps]
  exact monotone (subset_univ _)

/-- The syntactic model: an expression is identified only with itself. -/
def syntactic : Congruence Base Const where
  rel := Eq
  equivalence := ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun same => same.symm, fun first second => first.trans second⟩
  compatible := by
    intro e e' step
    induction step with
    | root same => exact same
    | piDomain _ ih => rw [ih]
    | piBody _ ih => rw [ih]
    | lamDomain _ ih => rw [ih]
    | lamBody _ ih => rw [ih]
    | appFunction _ ih => rw [ih]
    | appArgument _ ih => rw [ih]
    | andLeft _ ih => rw [ih]
    | andRight _ ih => rw [ih]
    | orLeft _ ih => rw [ih]
    | orRight _ ih => rw [ih]
    | impLeft _ ih => rw [ih]
    | impRight _ ih => rw [ih]
    | notBody _ ih => rw [ih]
    | eqLeft _ ih => rw [ih]
    | eqRight _ ih => rw [ih]
    | allDomain _ ih => rw [ih]
    | allBody _ ih => rw [ih]
    | exDomain _ ih => rw [ih]
    | exBody _ ih => rw [ih]

/-- The syntactic model is a strict model of a bubble exactly when the bubble
converts no two distinct expressions. -/
theorem syntactic_mem_models_iff {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop} :
    syntactic ∈ models strictSat (equations rules) ↔
      ∀ e e' : Expr Base Const, Convertible rules e e' → e = e' :=
  mem_models_equations

/-- **The global judgment is strictly weaker than every bubble that converts two
distinct expressions.** -/
theorem models_ssubset_noSteps {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {e e' : Expr Base Const} (converted : Convertible rules e e') (distinct : e ≠ e') :
    models strictSat (equations rules) ⊂ models strictSat (equations noSteps) := by
  rw [models_noSteps]
  refine ssubset_iff_subset_not_subset.mpr ⟨subset_univ _, fun included => distinct ?_⟩
  exact syntactic_mem_models_iff.mp (included (mem_univ syntactic)) e e' converted

/-- Conversely (classically), a bubble whose strict models are strictly fewer
than the global judgment's converts two distinct expressions. -/
theorem exists_distinct_of_models_ssubset {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    (strict : models strictSat (equations rules) ⊂ models strictSat (equations noSteps)) :
    ∃ e e' : Expr Base Const, Convertible rules e e' ∧ e ≠ e' := by
  rw [models_noSteps] at strict
  by_contra none
  apply (ssubset_iff_subset_not_subset.mp strict).2
  intro θ _
  refine mem_models_equations.mpr fun e e' converted => ?_
  have same : e = e' := by
    by_contra distinct
    exact none ⟨e, e', converted, distinct⟩
  rw [same]
  exact θ.equivalence.refl e'

/-! ## The degenerate model -/

/-- The congruence identifying everything. -/
def total : Congruence Base Const where
  rel := fun _ _ => True
  equivalence := ⟨fun _ => trivial, fun _ => trivial, fun _ _ => trivial⟩
  compatible := fun _ => trivial

/-- Every equation holds in the total congruence. -/
theorem total_strictSat (φ : Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const) : strictSat total φ :=
  trivial

/-- **The theory of all equations has exactly one strict model, the one that
identifies everything.** -/
theorem models_univ_eq_total :
    models strictSat (Set.univ : Set (Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const)) = {total} := by
  ext θ
  constructor
  · intro model
    apply Congruence.ext
    funext e e'
    exact propext ⟨fun _ => trivial, fun _ => model (mem_univ (e, e'))⟩
  · rintro rfl
    exact fun φ _ => total_strictSat φ

/-- The total congruence is a strict model of every bubble. -/
theorem total_mem_models (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    total ∈ models strictSat (equations rules) :=
  fun φ _ => total_strictSat φ

/-! ## Every type inhabited -/

/-- **The theory that every type is inhabited changes no conversion of a
bubble.** -/
theorem conversion_unchanged_by_inhabitation_top
    {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop} {e e' : Expr Base Const} :
    Entails (sumSat strictSat inhabitedSat)
        (sumTheory (equations rules) (Set.univ : Set (Expr Base Const))) (.inl (e, e')) ↔
      Convertible rules e e' :=
  permissive_top_conservative.trans convertible_iff_entails.symm

/-- It entails that the empty proposition is inhabited. -/
theorem inhabitation_top_inhabits_bot (rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    Entails (sumSat strictSat inhabitedSat)
      (sumTheory (equations rules) (Set.univ : Set (Expr Base Const))) (.inr Expr.bot) :=
  permissive_top_inhabits Expr.bot

/-! ## Strict against propositional -/

/-- **A justified bubble is invisible to the propositional theory and visible to
the strict one.**  Let `intended` be a class of strict models in which every
step of the bubble holds.  Adding the bubble's equations to the theory of
`intended` leaves its model class unchanged, while the bubble's own strict
models are strictly fewer than the global judgment's as soon as it converts two
distinct expressions. -/
theorem justified_bubble_propositionally_invisible
    {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    {intended : Set (Congruence Base Const)}
    (justified : ∀ φ ∈ equations rules, ∀ θ ∈ intended, strictSat θ φ)
    {e e' : Expr Base Const} (converted : Convertible rules e e') (distinct : e ≠ e') :
    models strictSat (theoryOf strictSat intended ∪ equations rules) =
        models strictSat (theoryOf strictSat intended) ∧
      models strictSat (equations rules) ⊂ models strictSat (equations noSteps) := by
  refine ⟨?_, models_ssubset_noSteps converted distinct⟩
  rw [models_union]
  apply inter_eq_left.mpr
  intro θ model φ rule
  exact model (fun θ' member => justified φ rule θ' member)

/-! ## The weakest sufficient bubble -/

/-- **The weakest theory meeting a set of required conversions is the
conversion generated by exactly those requirements.** -/
theorem isWeakestAdmissible_obligations
    (required : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop) :
    IsWeakestAdmissible strictSat (entailing strictSat (equations required))
      {φ : Expr Base Const × Expr Base Const | Convertible required φ.1 φ.2} := by
  rw [← consequences_equations]
  exact isWeakestAdmissible_entailing strictSat (equations required)

/-- A typing judgment of the core. -/
structure Judgment (Base : Type u) (Const : Ty Base → Type v) where
  ctx : List (Expr Base Const)
  term : Expr Base Const
  type : Expr Base Const

/-- The conversion obligations of a program: from the global type of each of
its terms to the type the program asks for. -/
def obligations (program : Set (Judgment Base Const)) :
    Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop :=
  fun A B => ∃ j ∈ program, HasType j.ctx j.term A ∧ j.type = B

/-- A bubble types a program whose terms are globally typed exactly when it
converts every obligation of the program. -/
theorem typesProgram_iff {program : Set (Judgment Base Const)}
    (typable : ∀ j ∈ program, ∃ A, HasType j.ctx j.term A)
    {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop} :
    (∀ j ∈ program, HasTypeIn rules j.ctx j.term j.type) ↔
      ∀ A B : Expr Base Const, obligations program A B → Convertible rules A B := by
  constructor
  · rintro types A B ⟨j, member, typing, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨A₀, typing₀, converted⟩ := hasTypeIn_iff.mp (types j member)
    rw [typing.unique typing₀]
    exact converted
  · intro discharged j member
    obtain ⟨A, typing⟩ := typable j member
    exact hasTypeIn_iff.mpr ⟨A, typing, discharged A j.type ⟨j, member, typing, rfl⟩⟩

/-- **The obligation bubble types the program.** -/
theorem obligationBubble_types {program : Set (Judgment Base Const)}
    (typable : ∀ j ∈ program, ∃ A, HasType j.ctx j.term A) :
    ∀ j ∈ program, HasTypeIn (obligations program) j.ctx j.term j.type :=
  (typesProgram_iff typable).mpr fun _ _ obligation =>
    Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root obligation)

/-- **The obligation bubble is the weakest bubble typing the program**: every
bubble that types it has no more strict models. -/
theorem obligationBubble_weakest {program : Set (Judgment Base Const)}
    (typable : ∀ j ∈ program, ∃ A, HasType j.ctx j.term A)
    {rules : Expr Base Const → Expr Base Const → Prop}
    (types : ∀ j ∈ program, HasTypeIn rules j.ctx j.term j.type) :
    models strictSat (equations rules) ⊆ models strictSat (equations (obligations program)) :=
  fun _ model _ obligation =>
    rel_of_convertible model ((typesProgram_iff typable).mp types _ _ obligation)

end Core

/-! ## Controls on the arithmetic bubbles -/

namespace ArithControl

open Mettapedia.TypeTheory.BubbleConversion.Arith

/-- The left-unit equation alone. -/
inductive LeftUnit : AExpr → AExpr → Prop where
  | zeroAdd (t : AExpr) : LeftUnit (addE zeroE t) t

/-- Contract a sum whose first summand is zero. -/
def appNormLeft (f a : AExpr) : AExpr :=
  match f with
  | app (const _ .add) (const _ .zero) => a
  | _ => app f a

/-- The normal form for the left-unit equation alone. -/
def normLeft : AExpr → AExpr
  | .bvar i => .bvar i
  | .univ => .univ
  | .prop => .prop
  | .base b => .base b
  | .pi A B => .pi (normLeft A) (normLeft B)
  | .lam A b => .lam (normLeft A) (normLeft b)
  | .app f a => appNormLeft (normLeft f) (normLeft a)
  | .const τ c => .const τ c
  | .tyFam b => .tyFam b
  | .top => .top
  | .bot => .bot
  | .and p q => .and (normLeft p) (normLeft q)
  | .or p q => .or (normLeft p) (normLeft q)
  | .imp p q => .imp (normLeft p) (normLeft q)
  | .not p => .not (normLeft p)
  | .eq a b => .eq (normLeft a) (normLeft b)
  | .all A b => .all (normLeft A) (normLeft b)
  | .ex A b => .ex (normLeft A) (normLeft b)

/-- The normal form of each arithmetic bubble, as a strict model. -/
def normModel (plus : Bool) : Congruence Unit ArithConst where
  rel := fun e e' => norm plus e = norm plus e'
  equivalence := ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun same => same.symm, fun first second => first.trans second⟩
  compatible := fun step => rewrite_norm plus (fun _ _ same => same) step

/-- The left-unit normal form, as a strict model. -/
def leftModel : Congruence Unit ArithConst where
  rel := fun e e' => normLeft e = normLeft e'
  equivalence := ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun same => same.symm, fun first second => first.trans second⟩
  compatible := by
    intro e e' step
    induction step with
    | root same => exact same
    | piDomain _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | piBody _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | lamDomain _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | lamBody _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | appFunction _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | appArgument _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | andLeft _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | andRight _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | orLeft _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | orRight _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | impLeft _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | impRight _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | notBody _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | eqLeft _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | eqRight _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | allDomain _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | allBody _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | exDomain _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]
    | exBody _ ih => simp only [normLeft, ih]

theorem normModel_mem : normModel false ∈ models strictSat (equations Rule) :=
  fun _ rule => rule_norm false rule

theorem leftModel_mem : leftModel ∈ models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) := by
  rintro ⟨left, right⟩ rule
  change LeftUnit left right at rule
  cases rule
  rfl

/-- A context holding a vector of length zero. -/
def zeroVecContext : List AExpr := [vec zeroE]

theorem zeroVec_typed : HasType zeroVecContext (bvar 0) (vec zeroE) :=
  HasType.var (Γ := zeroVecContext) (i := 0) rfl

/-- A program that uses a vector of length zero at length `0 + 0`. -/
def zeroVecProgram : Set (Judgment Unit ArithConst) :=
  {⟨zeroVecContext, bvar 0, vec (addE zeroE zeroE)⟩}

theorem zeroVecProgram_typable :
    ∀ j ∈ zeroVecProgram, ∃ A, HasType j.ctx j.term A := by
  rintro j rfl
  exact ⟨_, zeroVec_typed⟩

/-- The recursion equations type the program. -/
theorem arith_types_zeroVec :
    ∀ j ∈ zeroVecProgram, HasTypeIn Rule j.ctx j.term j.type := by
  rintro j rfl
  exact hasTypeIn_iff.mpr ⟨_, zeroVec_typed, (conv_iff_norm false).mpr rfl⟩

/-- The left-unit equation alone types the program. -/
theorem leftUnit_types_zeroVec :
    ∀ j ∈ zeroVecProgram, HasTypeIn LeftUnit j.ctx j.term j.type := by
  rintro j rfl
  refine hasTypeIn_iff.mpr ⟨_, zeroVec_typed, ?_⟩
  exact Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _
    (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.appArgument (Rewrite.root (LeftUnit.zeroAdd zeroE))))

/-- The left-unit bubble converts `0 + n` to `n`; the recursion equations do not. -/
theorem leftUnit_not_within_arith :
    ¬ models strictSat (equations Rule) ⊆ models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) := by
  intro included
  have converted : Convertible LeftUnit (addE zeroE (bvar 0)) (bvar 0) :=
    Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root (LeftUnit.zeroAdd (bvar 0)))
  have equal := mem_models_equations.mp (included normModel_mem) _ _ converted
  simp [normModel, norm, appNorm, addNorm, addE, zeroE] at equal

/-- The recursion equations convert `n + 0` to `n`; the left-unit bubble does not. -/
theorem arith_not_within_leftUnit :
    ¬ models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) ⊆ models strictSat (equations Rule) := by
  intro included
  have converted : Convertible Rule (addE (bvar 0) zeroE) (bvar 0) :=
    Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root (Rule.addZero (bvar 0)))
  have equal := mem_models_equations.mp (included leftModel_mem) _ _ converted
  simp [leftModel, normLeft, appNormLeft, addE, zeroE] at equal

/-- **Within the family of the two arithmetic bubbles there is no weakest
sufficient bubble**: both type the program, and neither has all the strict
models of the other. -/
theorem no_weakest_sufficient_in_family :
    (∀ j ∈ zeroVecProgram, HasTypeIn Rule j.ctx j.term j.type) ∧
      (∀ j ∈ zeroVecProgram, HasTypeIn LeftUnit j.ctx j.term j.type) ∧
      ¬ models strictSat (equations Rule) ⊆ models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) ∧
      ¬ models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) ⊆ models strictSat (equations Rule) :=
  ⟨arith_types_zeroVec, leftUnit_types_zeroVec, leftUnit_not_within_arith,
    arith_not_within_leftUnit⟩

/-- **The obligation bubble is strictly weaker than both**: it has all their
strict models, and each of them misses one of its strict models. -/
theorem obligation_strictly_weaker :
    models strictSat (equations Rule) ⊂ models strictSat (equations (obligations zeroVecProgram)) ∧
      models strictSat (equations LeftUnit) ⊂
        models strictSat (equations (obligations zeroVecProgram)) := by
  have leftIn : leftModel ∈ models strictSat (equations (obligations zeroVecProgram)) :=
    obligationBubble_weakest zeroVecProgram_typable leftUnit_types_zeroVec leftModel_mem
  have normIn : normModel false ∈ models strictSat (equations (obligations zeroVecProgram)) :=
    obligationBubble_weakest zeroVecProgram_typable arith_types_zeroVec normModel_mem
  refine ⟨ssubset_iff_subset_not_subset.mpr
      ⟨obligationBubble_weakest zeroVecProgram_typable arith_types_zeroVec, fun included => ?_⟩,
    ssubset_iff_subset_not_subset.mpr
      ⟨obligationBubble_weakest zeroVecProgram_typable leftUnit_types_zeroVec,
        fun included => ?_⟩⟩
  · have equal := mem_models_equations.mp (included leftIn) _ _
      (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root (Rule.addZero (bvar 0))))
    simp [leftModel, normLeft, appNormLeft, addE, zeroE] at equal
  · have equal := mem_models_equations.mp (included normIn) _ _
      (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root (LeftUnit.zeroAdd (bvar 0))))
    simp [normModel, norm, appNorm, addNorm, addE, zeroE] at equal

/-- The arithmetic bubble is invisible to the theory of its own normal-form
semantics extended by the left unit, and strictly stronger than the global
judgment. -/
theorem arith_invisible_but_strict :
    models strictSat (theoryOf strictSat {normModel true} ∪ equations Rule) =
        models strictSat (theoryOf strictSat {normModel true}) ∧
      models strictSat (equations Rule) ⊂ models strictSat (equations noSteps) := by
  refine justified_bubble_propositionally_invisible ?_
    (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root (Rule.addZero (bvar 0)))) ?_
  · rintro φ rule θ rfl
    exact rule_norm true rule
  · simp [addE, zeroE]

/-! ### Obligations are not stable under substitution -/

/-- The program that uses `v : Vec n` at `Vec (n + 0)`. -/
def vecProgram : Set (Judgment Unit ArithConst) :=
  {⟨vecContext, bvar 0, vec (addE (bvar 1) zeroE)⟩}

/-- Contract a sum of the variable `1` and zero, and nothing else. -/
def appNormVar (f a : AExpr) : AExpr :=
  match f, a with
  | app (const _ .add) (bvar 1), const _ .zero => bvar 1
  | _, _ => app f a

/-- The normal form for the single equation `x₁ + 0 = x₁`. -/
def normVar : AExpr → AExpr
  | .bvar i => .bvar i
  | .univ => .univ
  | .prop => .prop
  | .base b => .base b
  | .pi A B => .pi (normVar A) (normVar B)
  | .lam A b => .lam (normVar A) (normVar b)
  | .app f a => appNormVar (normVar f) (normVar a)
  | .const τ c => .const τ c
  | .tyFam b => .tyFam b
  | .top => .top
  | .bot => .bot
  | .and p q => .and (normVar p) (normVar q)
  | .or p q => .or (normVar p) (normVar q)
  | .imp p q => .imp (normVar p) (normVar q)
  | .not p => .not (normVar p)
  | .eq a b => .eq (normVar a) (normVar b)
  | .all A b => .all (normVar A) (normVar b)
  | .ex A b => .ex (normVar A) (normVar b)

/-- That normal form, as a strict model. -/
def varModel : Congruence Unit ArithConst where
  rel := fun e e' => normVar e = normVar e'
  equivalence := ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun same => same.symm, fun first second => first.trans second⟩
  compatible := by
    intro e e' step
    induction step with
    | root same => exact same
    | piDomain _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | piBody _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | lamDomain _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | lamBody _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | appFunction _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | appArgument _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | andLeft _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | andRight _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | orLeft _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | orRight _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | impLeft _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | impRight _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | notBody _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | eqLeft _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | eqRight _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | allDomain _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | allBody _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | exDomain _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]
    | exBody _ ih => simp only [normVar, ih]

theorem varModel_mem : varModel ∈ models strictSat (equations (obligations vecProgram)) := by
  rintro ⟨left, right⟩ ⟨j, member, typing, same⟩
  change j = _ at member
  subst member
  change HasType vecContext (bvar 0) left at typing
  change vec (addE (bvar 1) zeroE) = right at same
  have typeIs : left = vec (bvar 1) := (vecVariable_typed.unique typing).symm
  subst typeIs
  subst same
  rfl

/-- **The obligation bubble is not stable under substitution**: it converts
`Vec n` and `Vec (n + 0)`, but not their instances at `n := 0`. -/
theorem obligation_not_substitution_stable :
    Convertible (obligations vecProgram) (vec (bvar 1)) (vec (addE (bvar 1) zeroE)) ∧
      ¬ Convertible (obligations vecProgram) (substAt 1 zeroE (vec (bvar 1)))
        (substAt 1 zeroE (vec (addE (bvar 1) zeroE))) := by
  constructor
  · exact Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Rewrite.root ⟨_, rfl, vecVariable_typed, rfl⟩)
  · intro converted
    have same := rel_of_convertible varModel_mem converted
    simp [varModel, normVar, appNormVar, vec, addE, zeroE, substAt, shiftN, shiftAt] at same

end ArithControl

end Mettapedia.TypeTheory.BubbleWeakness
